Make one pass over the array, tracking the running sum, the minimum and the maximum. Subtract the minimum and maximum from the sum, then divide by `n - 2`. This is valid because all salaries are unique and `n >= 3`, so exactly one minimum and one maximum are excluded and at least one salary remains.

```typescript
function average(salary: number[]): number {
    let sum = 0;
    let mn = Infinity;
    let mx = -Infinity;
    for (const s of salary) {
        sum += s;
        if (s < mn) mn = s;
        if (s > mx) mx = s;
    }
    return (sum - mn - mx) / (salary.length - 2);
};
```

