I'll use lazy increments so every operation runs in O(1).

**Approach**
- Keep the values in a `stack` array, plus an `inc` array of the same length.
- `inc[i]` holds a pending increment that applies to the element at index `i` and every element below it.
- `increment(k, val)`: let `idx = min(k, size) - 1`. If the stack is not empty, add `val` to `inc[idx]`.
- `pop()`:
  - Read the top index `i` and its pending increment `inc[i]`.
  - The returned value is `stack[i] + inc[i]`.
  - Pass `inc[i]` down by adding it to `inc[i - 1]`, if that index exists.
  - Reset `inc[i]` to 0 and remove the top element.
- `push(x)`: if the stack is below `maxSize`, append `x` and append a pending increment of 0.

```typescript
class CustomStack {
    private stack: number[];
    private incs: number[];
    private maxSize: number;

    constructor(maxSize: number) {
        this.maxSize = maxSize;
        this.stack = [];
        this.incs = [];
    }

    push(x: number): void {
        if (this.stack.length < this.maxSize) {
            this.stack.push(x);
            this.incs.push(0);
        }
    }

    pop(): number {
        const n = this.stack.length;
        if (n === 0) return -1;
        const i = n - 1;
        const add = this.incs[i];
        const res = this.stack[i] + add;
        if (i > 0) this.incs[i - 1] += add;
        this.stack.pop();
        this.incs.pop();
        return res;
    }

    increment(k: number, val: number): void {
        const idx = Math.min(k, this.stack.length) - 1;
        if (idx >= 0) this.incs[idx] += val;
    }
}
```

