Approach:
1. Remove all dashes from `s` and convert it to uppercase.
2. If nothing is left, return an empty string.
3. The first group takes the leftover characters: its length is `len % k`, or `k` when `len` divides evenly. This keeps it non-empty and no longer than `k`.
4. Every remaining group takes exactly `k` characters.
5. Join the groups with dashes.

This runs in O(n) time.

```typescript
function licenseKeyFormatting(s: string, k: number): string {
    const clean = s.replace(/-/g, "").toUpperCase();
    const n = clean.length;
    if (n === 0) return "";
    const parts: string[] = [];
    let first = n % k;
    if (first === 0) first = k;
    parts.push(clean.substring(0, first));
    for (let i = first; i < n; i += k) {
        parts.push(clean.substring(i, i + k));
    }
    return parts.join("-");
};
```

