traces.inference_trace:
Approach: for each initially infected node `u`, find the uninfected nodes that only `u` can reach. Removing `u` saves exactly those nodes.

1. Mark every node in `initial` as infected.
2. From each infected node `u`, run a BFS that never steps onto another infected node. This collects all uninfected nodes `u` can reach without passing through other infected nodes.
3. For each uninfected node `v`, count how many distinct infected sources reach it.
4. A node `v` reached by exactly one source `u` is saved when `u` is removed. Count these per source.
5. Pick the source with the largest saved count. On ties, pick the smallest index, so sort `initial` before scanning.

This is valid because removing `u` takes away `u` itself and its edges. Any uninfected node still reachable from another infected node stays infected. A node reachable only through `u` is no longer infected.

Complexity: each BFS costs O(n²) on the adjacency matrix, so the total is O(k·n²) for `k` initial nodes. With n = 300 that is at most about 27 million steps, which is fine.

```typescript
function minMalwareSpread(graph: number[][], initial: number[]): number {
    const n = graph.length;
    const infected = new Array(n).fill(false);
    for (const u of initial) infected[u] = true;
    const reachCount = new Array(n).fill(0);
    const reachers: number[][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) reachers.push([]);
    for (const u of initial) {
        const seen = new Array(n).fill(false);
        seen[u] = true;
        const queue: number[] = [u];
        let head = 0;
        while (head < queue.length) {
            const x = queue[head++];
            const row = graph[x];
            for (let y = 0; y < n; y++) {
                if (row[y] === 1 && !seen[y] && !infected[y]) {
                    seen[y] = true;
                    queue.push(y);
                }
            }
        }
        for (let v = 0; v < n; v++) {
            if (seen[v] && v !== u) {
                reachCount[v]++;
                reachers[v].push(u);
            }
        }
    }
    const saved = new Map<number, number>();
    for (let v = 0; v < n; v++) {
        if (!infected[v] && reachCount[v] === 1) {
            const u = reachers[v][0];
            saved.set(u, (saved.get(u) || 0) + 1);
        }
    }
    const sorted = [...initial].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    let best = sorted[0];
    let bestVal = -1;
    for (const u of sorted) {
        const s = saved.get(u) || 0;
        if (s > bestVal) {
            bestVal = s;
            best = u;
        }
    }
    return best;
};
```

