traces.inference_trace:
Approach:

- If the string contains at most one `'0'`, no move can increase its value, so return it unchanged.
- Otherwise, let `first` be the index of the first `'0'` and `zeros` be the total count of `'0'`s.
- Operation 2 (`"10"` → `"01"`) lets us slide every zero at or after `first` leftward, so they all gather into one consecutive block starting at `first`.
- Operation 1 (`"00"` → `"10"`) then turns all but the last zero of that block into `'1'`.
- The single remaining `'0'` ends up at position `first + zeros - 1`, and every other character is `'1'`.

The result is a string of `n` ones with one `'0'` at that position. This runs in O(n).

```typescript
function maximumBinaryString(binary: string): string {
    const n = binary.length;
    let first = -1;
    let zeros = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (binary[i] === '0') {
            if (first === -1) first = i;
            zeros++;
        }
    }
    if (zeros <= 1) return binary;
    const pos = first + zeros - 1;
    return '1'.repeat(pos) + '0' + '1'.repeat(n - pos - 1);
};
```

