traces.inference_trace:
Precompute the compatibility score for every student-mentor pair. Then run a bitmask DP over the set of mentors already used.

- Let `dp[mask]` be the best total score after assigning the first `popcount(mask)` students to the mentors whose bits are set in `mask`.
- From each reachable `mask`, the next student is `i = popcount(mask)`.
- For every mentor `j` not in `mask`, update `dp[mask | (1 << j)]` with `dp[mask] + score[i][j]`.
- The answer is `dp[(1 << m) - 1]`, the state where every mentor is used.

With `m <= 8` there are at most 256 masks, so the work is about `2^m * m` transitions plus `m^2 * n` for the scores.

```typescript
function maxCompatibilitySum(students: number[][], mentors: number[][]): number {
    const m = students.length;
    const n = students[0].length;
    const score: number[][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {
        score.push([]);
        for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
            let s = 0;
            for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) if (students[i][k] === mentors[j][k]) s++;
            score[i].push(s);
        }
    }
    const full = 1 << m;
    const dp = new Array(full).fill(-1);
    dp[0] = 0;
    for (let mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
        if (dp[mask] < 0) continue;
        let i = 0;
        for (let t = mask; t; t &= t - 1) i++;
        if (i >= m) continue;
        for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
            if (mask & (1 << j)) continue;
            const nm = mask | (1 << j);
            dp[nm] = Math.max(dp[nm], dp[mask] + score[i][j]);
        }
    }
    return dp[full - 1];
};
```

