Memoised recursion: it is never worse to eat single oranges only until `n` becomes divisible by 2 or by 3, then take the big step.

- To use the halving step, first eat `n % 2` single oranges, then spend 1 day halving. Total: `n % 2 + 1 + f(n / 2)`.
- To use the thirding step, first eat `n % 3` single oranges, then spend 1 day reducing to a third. Total: `n % 3 + 1 + f(n / 3)`.
- So `f(n) = 1 + min(n % 2 + f(floor(n / 2)), n % 3 + f(floor(n / 3)))`.
- Base cases: `f(0) = 0` and `f(1) = 1`.

Only values of the form `floor(n / (2^a · 3^b))` are ever reached, so a `Map` cache keeps the number of states small (a few hundred at most).

