Approach: treat every pair of points as the two opposite corners of a diagonal, then check whether the other two corners exist.

1. Store every point in a set, encoded as the number `x * 40001 + y`. Coordinates are at most 40000, so the encoding is unique and stays below about 1.6e9, which fits safely in a JS number.
2. For each pair of points `(x1, y1)` and `(x2, y2)` with `x1 != x2` and `y1 != y2`, check whether `(x1, y2)` and `(x2, y1)` are both in the set.
3. If they are, the four points form an axis-parallel rectangle with area `|x1 - x2| * |y1 - y2|`. Keep the minimum.
4. If no rectangle is found, return 0.

With n = 500 there are about 125k pairs, each checked in O(1), so the total cost is O(n²).

```typescript
function minAreaRect(points: number[][]): number {
    const M = 40001;
    const set = new Set<number>();
    for (const [x, y] of points) set.add(x * M + y);
    let best = Infinity;
    const n = points.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const x1 = points[i][0], y1 = points[i][1];
        for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            const x2 = points[j][0], y2 = points[j][1];
            if (x1 === x2 || y1 === y2) continue;
            const area = Math.abs(x1 - x2) * Math.abs(y1 - y2);
            if (area >= best) continue;
            if (set.has(x1 * M + y2) && set.has(x2 * M + y1)) {
                best = area;
            }
        }
    }
    return best === Infinity ? 0 : best;
};
```

