Approach: BFS/DP over bitmasks of which target positions are already covered. With `target.length <= 15`, there are at most 2^15 = 32768 states.

1. For each sticker, count how many of each letter it has.
2. Let `dp[mask]` be the minimum number of stickers needed to cover the positions in `mask`. Start with `dp[0] = 0`; all other entries are `Infinity`.
3. Process masks in increasing order. Applying a sticker only adds bits, so every transition goes to a larger mask, and each mask is final when we reach it.
4. For a reachable mask, find the first uncovered position `i`. Only try stickers that contain `target[i]`. Some sticker must eventually cover that position, so this pruning is safe.
5. To apply a sticker, copy its letter counts. Then walk the uncovered positions and greedily mark each one whose letter is still available, decrementing the count. Update `dp[next] = min(dp[next], dp[mask] + 1)`.
6. The answer is `dp[full]`, or `-1` if it was never reached.

Cost: 32768 masks × 50 stickers × 15 positions is about 24M operations, which is fine.

```typescript
function minStickers(stickers: string[], target: string): number {
    const n = target.length;
    const full = (1 << n) - 1;
    const cnts: number[][] = stickers.map(s => {
        const c = new Array(26).fill(0);
        for (const ch of s) c[ch.charCodeAt(0) - 97]++;
        return c;
    });
    const t: number[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) t.push(target.charCodeAt(i) - 97);
    const dp = new Array(1 << n).fill(Infinity);
    dp[0] = 0;
    for (let mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
        if (dp[mask] === Infinity) continue;
        let first = 0;
        while ((mask >> first) & 1) first++;
        for (const c of cnts) {
            if (c[t[first]] === 0) continue;
            const cur = c.slice();
            let next = mask;
            for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if ((next >> i) & 1) continue;
                if (cur[t[i]] > 0) {
                    cur[t[i]]--;
                    next |= 1 << i;
                }
            }
            if (dp[mask] + 1 < dp[next]) dp[next] = dp[mask] + 1;
        }
    }
    return dp[full] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[full];
};
```

