traces.inference_trace:
Greedy approach: build the string one character at a time.

- At each step, write `'a'` if:
  - the last two characters are both `'b'` (writing `'b'` would create `"bbb"`), or
  - `a > b` and the last two characters are not both `'a'`.
- Otherwise write `'b'`.

This keeps the larger count shrinking fastest while never placing three equal letters in a row. The problem guarantees a valid string exists, so the greedy never gets stuck.

```typescript
function strWithout3a3b(a: number, b: number): string {
    const res: string[] = [];
    while (a > 0 || b > 0) {
        const n = res.length;
        let writeA: boolean;
        if (n >= 2 && res[n - 1] === res[n - 2]) {
            writeA = res[n - 1] === 'b';
        } else {
            writeA = a >= b;
        }
        if (writeA && a === 0) writeA = false;
        if (!writeA && b === 0) writeA = true;
        if (writeA) {
            res.push('a');
            a--;
        } else {
            res.push('b');
            b--;
        }
    }
    return res.join('');
};
```

